-- title:
--   Simultaneous local generators at finitely many maximal ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and $J \subseteq P$ an ideal, and suppose the set of ideals $\mathfrak{n}$ of $P$ that are maximal and contain $J$ is finite. Let $N$ be a natural number and assume that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{n} \supseteq J$ there is a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,N \to P$ with $g(i) \in J$ for all $i$ such that the image ideal $J \cdot \mathrm{Localization.AtPrime}\,\mathfrak{n}$ — that is, the ideal generated by the image of $J$ under the canonical map $P \to P_{\mathfrak{n}}$ — coincides with the ideal generated by the images of the $g(i)$. The conclusion is that the family may be chosen uniformly in $\mathfrak{n}$: there exists a single $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,N \to P$ with $f(i) \in J$ for all $i$ such that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{n} \supseteq J$ the ideal generated by the image of $J$ in $P_{\mathfrak{n}}$ equals the ideal generated by the images of $f(0), \dots, f(N-1)$ in $P_{\mathfrak{n}}$. The number $N$ of generators is thus the same globally as it is locally at each of the finitely many relevant maximal ideals.
--
--   This is a local–global statement on the number of generators of an ideal: finitely many local presentations by $N$ elements of $J$ can be realised by one $N$-tuple in $J$ simultaneously. It is used in [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers) to pass from pointwise local generators to a single global presentation of an ideal with a prescribed number of generators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_forall_map_localization_eq_span_of_finite_maximal.lean

